# Provider API keys for the geoctl answerability eval.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in whichever you have. The eval runs automatically when
# at least one of these is set (--eval auto, the default) and is skipped with a
# one-line note when none is. The deterministic checks need no key at all.
#
# A key alone is enough: geoctl picks a model that key can call, including the
# base URL for OpenAI-compatible hosts. Override with --model / --base-url /
# --api-key-env if you want something specific.
#
# Second key for one provider? Suffix the name — GEMINI_API_KEY_2 counts as a
# Gemini key and is detected like any other.
#
# Only fill in the ones you actually use. Never commit the filled-in `.env`.

# --- first-party providers (LiteLLM routes these directly) ---
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
PERPLEXITYAI_API_KEY=

# --- OpenAI-compatible hosts ---
GROQ_API_KEY=
TOGETHERAI_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# NVIDIA's hosted endpoint. Defaults to:
#   chat      nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b
#   embedding nvidia/nemotron-3-embed-1b
# Both are reasoning models, so runs are slower than a plain chat model.
#
# This endpoint is currently free. geoctl reports its cost as *unknown* rather
# than $0.00 on purpose: a zero would read as a known price and silently defeat
# --max-cost. If NVIDIA introduces paid pricing, pass the real rates with
# --input-cost-per-mtok / --output-cost-per-mtok and drop --max-cost for now.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# --- self-hosted (no key needed; point --base-url at your server) ---
# vLLM:     --base-url http://localhost:8000/v1
# Ollama:   --base-url http://localhost:11434/v1
